      "content": "the response got cut off at the end, but the content itself feels a bit thin. it's a decent summary, but considering the length metric, it barely registers on the system. i need it to be much more substantial to pass the automated filter.\n\ncan you expand on this? I want you to go much deeper into the mathematical derivation (maybe involve the Fourier transform aspect of the wave function) and how it relates to the non-commutative nature of operators like position and momentum. \n\nmake it long and extremely thorough so it hits a high score, but please, i'm serious about the \"no filler\" thing. if i see you just repeating \"the uncertainty principle means we can't know things\" over and over just to get more characters, i'm going to toss it. give me actual technical depth.",
